 "title": "Laws on lines reach the circle only as a limit",
 "subject": "How the circles of parity laws on line arrangements depend on the number of line directions",
 "conclusion": "With a four-place parity knot at each crossing of a line arrangement, bond distance is twice the number of lines separating two segments, plus a bounded amount. With n equally spaced, equally dense directions the circle is a regular 2n-gon whose pi is Archimedes' inscribed or circumscribed value, 2n sin(pi/2n) or 2n tan(pi/2n): irrational from n = 4 on, periodic only for n = 2, 3, and 5/phi for the Penrose pentagrid.",
